   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to nursing home and assisted living facility disaster preparedness plans",
    "basePrintNo": "S5838",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5838-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23-b, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5838\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to nursing home and\nassisted living facility disaster preparedness plans\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis bill would relate to disaster preparedness plans for nursing\nhomes and assisted living facilities.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection One of the bill adds a new subdivision 4 to Section 23-b of\nthe executive law to clarify that the measure preserves existing\nregulatory authority in this area of state public policy.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis chapter amendment would clarify that the new law shall not be\ndeemed to modify or override duly promulgated regulations, or to limit\nthe authority to promulgate regulations in the future, with respect to\ndisaster preparedness of such facilities, the contents of their\ndisaster preparedness plans or the process for approval of those\nplans.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is a Chapter Amendment to Chapter 589 of the Laws of 2008.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediate, and shall be deemed to have been in full force and effect\non and after the effective date of Chapter 589 of the Laws of 2008.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
